>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `Iff`

``` hol4
clasetLib.Iff : thm -> thm
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Marks a theorem as a temporary iff declaration for a clasimp tactic.

`Iff th` is logically equivalent to `th`, but carries a marker recognized
by the theorem-list clasimp tactics. For that invocation, the theorem is
added as a rewrite and also contributes classical rules using the same
decision tree as `[iff]`: equivalences produce an intro/dest pair,
negations produce an elimination rule, and other propositions produce an
introduction rule. Derived rules are safe exactly when the source has no
implication antecedents.

The theorem is not inserted as an assumption, and neither derived view
survives the tactic call. Use `[iff]` for a persistent declaration.

Classical-only and tableau tactics have no simpset and reject `Iff`.

### Failure

Constructing `Iff th` does not validate the declaration. A consuming
clasimp tactic can fail during rule or rewrite conversion. Classical-only
and tableau tactics reject the marker.

### Example

``` hol4
clasimpLib.AUTO_TAC [clasetLib.Iff my_equivalence]
```

